# RME invoice correction — pilot IDENTITY restriction + payment explicit ACTOR (rule 197)

Evidence: `docs/sprints/hardening-rme-invoice-correction-pilot-identity-payment-actor-1.md`.
Decisions: `docs/decisions/rme-billing-correction-owner-decisions.md` (D1e).
Extends rule 195 (activation contract) and rule 196 (verification ladder).
**Supersedes rule 196 §13**, which said D1d was "a designation, not an allowlist":
since D1e it IS an enforced allowlist. Where rule 195 §5/§20 says Front Office
holds request+approve, that remains true of the ROLE; inside the pilot only the
two designated accounts may use it.

## A. Owner decision D1e — who may act in the pilot

1. Recorded `OWNER_POLICY_APPROVED` 2026-10-21 (owner instruction in this sprint's
   brief). It is an owner decision: never widen, narrow or reinterpret it without
   a new one recorded in the register first.
2. | Action | Allowed | Everyone else |
   |---|---|---|
   | SUBMIT | maker `29` | `PILOT_IDENTITY_NOT_AUTHORIZED` |
   | APPROVE (= apply, D1a) | checker `1` | refused |
   | REJECT | checker `1` | refused |
   | APPLY (recovery path) | checker `1` | refused |
   | CANCEL own correction | the correction's own maker | `NOT_THE_MAKER` |
3. Relation to D1a–D1d: D1a (approve applies) unchanged; D1b (Front Office holds
   request+approve) unchanged for the ROLE and narrowed by identity inside the
   pilot; D1c (SPN4) unchanged — WHERE; D1e — WHO. D1d named the accounts; D1e
   makes them the only ones.
4. Role permissions are NOT changed by D1e. `RoleSeeder` stays at its rule-195
   grants (production 514 role-permission pairs). Never "implement" an identity
   restriction by editing roles, pins, cohorts or `role_has_permissions`.
5. Super Admin is NOT exempt. `Gate::before` returns true for every policy for a
   Super Admin, so a policy can never be this control. A second Super Admin is
   refused exactly like a second Front Office account.

## B. Where it is enforced
6. `RmeInvoiceCorrectionPilotIdentity` is the single authority. The SERVICE
   (`RmeInvoiceCorrectionService`) asserts it inside the transaction, after the
   row lock, for submit / approve / reject / recovery apply. A command, job or
   future controller therefore cannot reach a transition around it.
7. Order inside the lock (each refuses on its own; the order only decides which
   code is reported): flag → permission + working-branch scope → branch allowlist
   (submit/approve/apply) → self-decision (`SELF_APPROVAL` / `SELF_APPLICATION`) →
   identity. A self-approval keeps its own code; an out-of-branch caller keeps the
   404/`BRANCH_OUT_OF_SCOPE` that reveals nothing.
8. The policy repeats identity for approve/reject/apply (a courtesy for non-Super-
   Admin accounts). The controller answers the request form/store with **403** for
   a non-designated account — asked AFTER the branch-scope 404. The detail page
   renders decision controls from `RmeInvoiceCorrectionService::actionsFor()`
   (explicit identity check), never from a bare `@can`, because `@can` is true for
   any Super Admin. The cashier panel's `can_request` includes the identity.
9. Read access (list, detail, frozen document versions, the approvals list) stays
   governed by the existing permissions and branch scope. Hiding a control is a
   courtesy; the service is the control.

## C. The allowlist — source-controlled and fail-closed
10. `config/rme_invoice_correction.php` → `pilot.identities` =
    `['maker_user_ids' => [29], 'checker_user_ids' => [1]]`. NO `env()` — the
    cohort is an owner decision that arrives as a reviewed commit. A governance
    test pins the exact shipped values; changing them must fail CI until the test
    and the decision register change in the same reviewed commit.
11. FAIL CLOSED: a missing key, a non-array, a non-list, a string id, a zero or a
    negative id voids the WHOLE allowlist (one unreadable entry is never skipped);
    overlapping lists void it (one account never holds both halves). Void = nobody
    may submit, approve, reject or recovery-apply.
12. An EMPTY role list is readable and stops that role only: empty makers = no new
    submissions while the checker still resolves filed corrections. SUBMIT also
    requires at least one designated checker — a correction nobody may decide
    would hold its invoice behind the D10 block.
13. The identity allowlist is independent of the branch allowlist: adding a branch
    to `pilot.branch_codes` does not widen who may act, and vice versa. Each is a
    separate owner decision.
14. The actor must be a PERSISTED, non-deleted, ACTIVE account, re-read from the
    database (`PILOT_IDENTITY_ACTOR_UNUSABLE` otherwise). An in-memory object
    carrying a designated id is not that account; a deactivation committed
    elsewhere is seen immediately.

## D. Release paths — never strand an invoice
15. CANCEL of one's own SUBMITTED/APPROVED correction is NOT identity-gated: it is
    the maker's de-escalation and the guaranteed release path. It stays confined
    to that one account (`NOT_THE_MAKER`), the request permission and the branch
    scope. Never gate it by the identity list.
16. REJECT is identity-gated (owner D1e) but NOT branch-gated (rule 195 §17).
17. The recovery APPLY (pre-D1a APPROVED rows; 0 in production) is the second half
    of an approval (D1a) and belongs to the checker identity. This NARROWS the
    apply permission (held by every Super Admin) to user 1, who already held it;
    it grants nobody anything new.
18. Every active correction keeps at least one release path whatever the lists
    say: its own maker's cancel; and while a checker is designated, the checker's
    reject. Tests pin both after a narrowing.
19. The flag remains the global kill switch — but cancel and reject are ALSO
    flag-gated, while D10 is NOT. So: resolve (reject/cancel) every active
    correction BEFORE switching the flag OFF, or the invoice stays payment-blocked
    until the flag returns (rule 195 §30).

## E. Payment — the EXPLICIT actor, never the ambient session
20. `RmePaymentService::assertInvoicePayable(RmeInvoice, User $cashier)` judges the
    cashier the caller passes — the account written to `cashier_id` — on every
    path (pay, control allocation, visit allocation all funnel through it).
21. Root cause fixed: it used `Auth::user()`. That judged the wrong person for any
    non-HTTP caller, and with NO session `RmeWorkingBranchScope::branchIdsFor(null)`
    answers EVERY active RME branch — the branch check failed OPEN.
22. The cashier must be a persisted, non-deleted, ACTIVE account (re-read). Every
    payment entry point declares a non-nullable `User $cashier`; there is no
    overload that omits it and no session fallback.
23. A governance test strips comments and asserts `RmePaymentService` contains no
    `Auth::`, `auth()` or `request()` in code. Never reintroduce one.
24. Unchanged by design: carry-over parents of a control/visit allocation are
    selected server-side by `RmeControlReceivableService` (patient-scoped, RME
    branches) and are NOT re-scoped to the cashier's working branch — that is the
    approved Sprint 62.2 cross-branch collection contract. Super Admin keeps its
    existing governance cashier scope (every active RME branch).
25. Preserved: D10 block under the invoice lock (rule 192), invoice-version binding
    (rule 191), future `paid_at` refusal, batch atomicity, manual pricing (rule 194).

## F. Readiness probe
26. `rme:invoice-correction-readiness` reports `PILOT_IDENTITIES valid=… maker=…
    checker=…`, a `Pilot identity` column per user, and FAILs on
    `PILOT_IDENTITY_CONFIG_INVALID`, `PAIR_MAKER_NOT_PILOT_IDENTITY`,
    `PAIR_CHECKER_NOT_PILOT_IDENTITY`; WATCHes on an empty role list. Run it only as
    the runtime user (rule 195 §28a).

## G. Production procedure (this sprint) and limits
27. Exposure found 2026-10-21 08:14 UTC: 8 Front Office accounts held both halves in
    SPN4. Mitigation before any code: flag OFF (one env line, inode/perms
    preserved, config cache as `daengtisiams`) after confirming 0 corrections.
28. The flag returns ON only after the deployed identity guard is verified on
    production. If verification fails, it stays OFF (NO_GO).
29. This sprint's GO tag certifies the HARDENING only. It does NOT certify
    `PILOT_LIVE`, `AUTHENTICATED_VERIFIED`, `FINANCIAL_CORRECTION_VERIFIED` or
    `FULL_ACTIVATION_GO` (rule 196) — those still need the real operators and a
    real, owner-authorized case. Never fabricate a session, invoice, payment or
    correction to produce evidence.
30. Recorded residual (not fixed here): `RmeWorkingBranchScope::branchIdsFor(null)`
    answers every RME branch, and `RmeInvoiceService::cashierScopeBranchIds()` still
    reads `Auth::user()` for cashier READ lists. Both are reached only from
    authenticated controllers today; changing the shared scope's null contract is a
    separate, wider change.
